# VACASK: SFFM defaults, $abstime, chgtol, the save caveat (062bcac0, part k).
# What the fix was for, as the ledger has it: `save v(in)` in the control block and
# `warning[caveat]` `save.signals: in VACASK's ac, noise, acxf and dcinc analyses v() saves the
# operating point; the small-signal value is dv() (docs/cmd-analysis-ac.md)`.
from: ngspice
to: vacask
--- input
t
V1 in 0 AC 1
R1 in 0 1k
.ac dec 4 10 10k
.save v(in)
.end
--- output
t
ground 0
load "spice/resistor.osdi"
model resistor sp_resistor
model vsource vsource
V1 (in 0) vsource mag=1
R1 (in 0) resistor r=1k
control
save v(in)
analysis ac1 ac from=10 to=10k mode="dec" points=4
endc
--- report
warning[caveat]: line 5: save.signals: in VACASK's ac, noise, acxf and dcinc analyses v() saves the operating point; the small-signal value is dv() (docs/cmd-analysis-ac.md)
warning[caveat]: line 4: ac.points: VACASK counts points per decade with no rounding tolerance and spaces a span that is not a whole number of steps evenly up to the stop, not on SPICE's per-decade grid
